{"name":"Rage","hex":"#ff1133","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rage","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Violent uncontrolled anger.","A current fashion or fad."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To act or speak in heightened anger.","To move with great violence, as a storm etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rage (emotion)","blocks":[{"text":"Rage is intense, uncontrolled anger that is an increased stage of hostile response to a perceived egregious injury or injustice."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Physiognomy.jpg/330px-Physiognomy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rage_(emotion)"},{"title":"Rage (Marvel Comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Rage is a fictional character appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. He has been a member of the Avengers and the New Warriors, and appeared in the pages of The Avengers, New Warriors, Night Thrasher, and Avengers: The Initiative. In the second volume of Night Thrasher, Haliday was reintroduced as The O.G., the leader of a small gang."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b2/Ragecomics.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rage_(Marvel_Comics)"},{"title":"Rage (music genre)","blocks":[{"text":"Rage is a subgenre of trap music that originated in the United States in the late 2010s. The early rage sound was characterized by short, looping, stereo-widened, future bass-influenced synthesizer lead hooks and basic, energetic trap rhythms. Among the early pioneers of rage rap were Playboi Carti, Lil Uzi Vert and Trippie Redd. Producer F1lthy helped develop a template for the style through his collective Working on Dying with members such as Bnyx."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rage_(music_genre)"},{"title":"Rage (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Rage is a first-person shooter video game developed by id Software and published by Bethesda Softworks, released in October 2011 for Microsoft Windows, the PlayStation 3, and the Xbox 360, and in February 2012 for OS X. It was first shown as a tech demo at the 2007 Apple Worldwide Developers Conference and was announced at the QuakeCon. Rage uses id Software's id Tech 5 game engine and is the final game released by the company under the supervision of founder John Carmack."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bd/Rage_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rage_(video_game)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/47-aspetti_di_vita_quotidiana%2Cira%2CTaccuino_Sanitatis%2C_Casana.jpg/500px-47-aspetti_di_vita_quotidiana%2Cira%2CTaccuino_Sanitatis%2C_Casana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/47-aspetti_di_vita_quotidiana%2Cira%2CTaccuino_Sanitatis%2C_Casana.jpg/500px-47-aspetti_di_vita_quotidiana%2Cira%2CTaccuino_Sanitatis%2C_Casana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rage, Tacuinum Sanitatis casanatensis (14th century).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A47-aspetti_di_vita_quotidiana%2Cira%2CTaccuino_Sanitatis%2C_Casana.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Rage-and-anger-fresco.jpg/500px-Rage-and-anger-fresco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Rage-and-anger-fresco.jpg/500px-Rage-and-anger-fresco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Angel with Temperance and Humility virtues versus Devil with Rage and Anger sins. A fresco from the 1717 Saint Nicholas churc